      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page describes a mechanism in the guarded write path that handles file state management and rollback. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\nAccording to [[pages/write-journal]], the Guarded Write Journal:\n\n1. **Records prior state**: Before overwriting any file, it records the file\u0027s previous state \u2014 either its prior content if it existed, or a note that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n2. **In-memory transaction log**: The journal is held in the process\u0027s memory during a single run and functions as a transaction log.\n\n3. **Rollback on failure**: If an agent run fails (due to turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order \u2014 restoring previous content for files that existed and deleting newly created files.\n\n4. **All-or-nothing semantics**: This approach provides all-or-nothing write semantics without requiring a database transaction.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses the journal\u0027s rollback functionality since it has no write tool of its own.",
